## Control of blood pressure and blood lipids

Blood pressure should be measured at every visit.

Hypertension treatment is indicated in people with diabetes when systolic blood pressure ≥130 mmHg or diastolic blood pressure ≥80 mmHg. Statins are recommended for all people with type 2 diabetes 40 years old or older, but only if this does not negatively impact access to glucose-lowering and blood pressurelowering medication.

